   210	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   211	    """
   212	    Use mirrored local legends to learn a stencil-backed two-color swap.
   213	
   214	    Input structure:
   215	    - Black background with isolated colored pixels and teal (8) stencil components.
   216	    - A usable rule is not a lone directed pair: the same teal component must be
   217	      flanked by reciprocal legends A->B and B->A that share one anchor region.
   218	      Unpaired legends may appear as distractors but do not activate any stencil.
   219	    - Away from the legend, isolated pixels may use either endpoint color of that
   220	      learned swap pair.
   221	
   222	    Rule:
   223	    - Keep only legend information that forms a bidirectional pair around one
   224	      stencil, then treat the two endpoint colors as a reversible mapping.
   225	    - For each non-legend A pixel, stamp the associated teal stencil at that pixel
   226	      recolored to B; for each non-legend B pixel, stamp the same stencil recolored
   227	      back to A.
   228	    - Remove all teal template pixels, and erase only the legend pixels that belong
   229	      to a validated reciprocal swap. Unpaired legend colors remain ordinary pixels.
   230	
   231	    Key insight: The reciprocal legend and the bidirectional execution describe the
   232	    same relationship, so one shared stencil encodes a visible A<->B exchange.
   233	    """
